      "title": "A flexible payment does not remove the monthly costs",
      "narration": "Elena owns universal life coverage and wants to reduce her payments while changing jobs. Universal life separates premium funding, interest credits, and policy deductions. The owner may have flexibility within the contract, but insurance costs and administrative charges continue. A planned premium is not automatically the amount guaranteed to sustain coverage forever. If payments and earnings do not support the deductions, the available value can decline. Without an applicable protection provision, insufficient funding can lead to lapse after the required process. First read the policy's funding conditions and current statement, then discuss the effect of the proposed change.",
