      "title": "Trace a simplified account for one month",
      "narration": "Use a deliberately simplified teaching account. It begins with one thousand dollars. A two-hundred-dollar payment adds one hundred ninety dollars after an assumed ten-dollar premium charge. Assume twenty dollars of interest is credited and one hundred thirty dollars of insurance and other charges are deducted. The ending value is one thousand eighty dollars. Now remove the payment while keeping the other assumptions fixed. The ending value becomes eight hundred ninety dollars. This example illustrates separate flows, not a real carrier's calculation order or guaranteed monthly return. Missing a payment does not make the insurance charges disappear.",
