      "title": "Review the policy instead of relying on a headline",
      "narration": "Elena should review the death-benefit option, current account and surrender values, deductions, premium history, and any guarantee's status. Some universal designs offer a level benefit, while others add the account value to a stated amount. Use the actual option and policy rules; do not assume every policy pays both amounts. Benefit increases may require new evidence of insurability. Request an updated in-force illustration using appropriate assumptions when reviewing future funding. Explain which figures are guaranteed and which are projections. A sound review connects the client's continuing protection need to an affordable funding plan and the contract's actual conditions.",
